{"title":"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Practice Relay Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Practice_Relay_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Zoe sold her old bicycle, skateboard, and ice skates for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/8/1382a05b7a5de75e75c7c4ce1139716e2a729d22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" />. If she sold the bicycle for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/8/318d0ebaa7b933b124efa3f5d5efc2eee9339232.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> and the skateboard for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfbe8755ab50447cac8dac1ef464e9d4034f110d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" />, how much did she get for the ice skates? \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Practice_Relay_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be how much she sold the ice skates for. Using the information from the problem, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa6a1b8b6b68062c1f5f2a10c8879b9270aabd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c + \\$35 + \\$25 = \\$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"159\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/9/179ade10884f03134dd80cc159b79aeb90fa325f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c + \\$60 = \\$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/e/71ea861333ef79832b4b481f6c10cda7adf80710.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = \\$N - \\$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Practice_Relay_Problem_2\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Practice Relay Problem 2\">player 2</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/4/9349c73dd92033b25035ca88db7d6cbca7dc32e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />. This means that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/b/e0bed11c4d9972443a2a638dd1b16e54c0dacf91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = \\$72 - \\$60 = \\boxed{\\$12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"174\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC\">2023 CEMC TUC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a 